This game was good some years ago, now is just.. outdated!
I tried the game just for fun and the nostalgia since i played back in the days this game was good.
Pros:
- Alot of classes;
- Can play all the classes with one character only;
- Can play more than 1 class at same which means you can create your own play style;
- Pets that can evolve;
Cons:
- Hotkeys sucks, honestly the only hotbar with hotkeys is the first one and is F1, F2, etc, can't change;
- 100% grind;
- Outdated graphics;
- Low amount of content comparing to other games;
- Resolution issues, i had to go directly to the files to change the resolution;
- Overall just an outdated game!
Im not saying the game is bad because it isn't but comparing to the games we see out there.. you know, this one can't compete with them, end of story.
I recommend this game?
Thats a hard question because i think you should try the game if you have nothing better to do and see by yourself but im not sure if it will be worth your time if you are playing current mmos.. like i said, give it a shot if you are bored and have nothing else to do!

The biggest con for this game is the time needed for each run. Count a couple hours easily.
As for the rest:
A good sountrack, nice pixelated graphics, good difficulty (even if it feels kind of unfair sometimes). Each one of my few runs were enjoyable. I think I'll expend on this review if I reach 25 hours or so, but I can already recommend this game to players who:
-like randomly generated dungeons (and the difficulty that generally comes with them);
-like turn-based games (which means you can take all the time you want to plan your next moves);
-like leveling, but don't mind if they don't really "grind" for it, and don't need to be able to reach lvl 100 to enjoy it;
-like equipements, but don't want to deal with 10+ simultaneous pieces of armor on your characters, or with the 100 variations of this "long sword+2";
-like resource management, but don't like headaches;
-like the placement choices inherent to tower defenses.
All those aspects of the game (rpg, td, management, etc.) mesh well together, bring a lot to the gameplay, but none of them is developed to the point of being unbearably cumbersome. If you want a full-fledged rpg/td/etc., you may have to look elsewhere.

