SUPERHOT is an FPS almost turn-based shooter made by SUPERHOT Team (6 polish people).
You may not like FPS or Turn-Based games ( I certantly don`t quite like TB games, with some exceptions) but you will certantly love this. Why? Simply because of the slow-motion combat mechanics and strategy involved in each level, since this game is level based and not a story-line driven game.
Just like the game itself say, all levels might seem random at first but it all comes togheder once you will have the patience (over 1,700 people who wrote bad reviews about this game certatly didn`t had) to reach the second half part of the game. I won`t spoil anything since  people already done that in other reviews and I also don`t want to ruin any surprises for someone who might try this game for first time without looking up on Internet for what it might be about in it.
I just want at point out, in the end of my review, some aspects that make this game very enjoyable:
*unussual and inovative menu;
*unique and origial story;
*slow-motion combat;
*ability to capture, edit and upload each level upon after you completed it;
*easy and obtainable achivements;
*sadisfactory game sounds (mostly the glass-breaking sounds and the SUPER-HOT at the end);
*simple and aestethic graphics;
What might put off some people are:
*slow story pacing, despite game being quite short (I completed it in 6 hr);
*ridiculously high price tag; should had been around 10$ at most;
3rd party key websites and sales are recommended if you want to buy this game.
Other than this, I really liked this game and hope that many people will, as well!

