I've been playing this game since ~2009. I really enjoyed it back then, but it all went to ♥♥♥♥ after 2012.
The overall gameplay was pretty cool. The controlls are different from other MMORPGs, which makes it feel unique in its own way. What I hate about this game is:
- boring leveling system: basically, you have to spend dozens of hours just killing monsters so you can level up;
- the story was pretty nice, but 98% of the quests were like ''go kill x in y map, then return to z''. A lot of them aren't even worth finishing;
- the weapons were nice, but pretty much any weapon between level 30 to 75 was taken over by lvl 30 weapons. I really hated how many weapons there were and they were a lot weaker than lvl 30 weapons. As if it wasn't enough, after 2012 update when they added bonus chests, the weapons from level 30 became even more powerful and cheaper. It was boring to play your way through dozens of levels with a single weapon;
- obvious pay to win;
- the Lycan update pretty much ruined the game even more than it already was. A cheap way of milking the players for money. An OP race that didn't fit in the story at all;
- the time you had to wait between reading a book, leveling up your horse skill and such. It made a bit of sense, but one day for a book that may or may not work? No, that was too much. 10 days just so I can  get a battle horse? It was simply frustrating;
- poorly chosen admins, who almost never even bother to take a look at the game. If you've played before 2014, you remember the dozens of hackers from map2. You couldn't even level up in such maps because of all the bots;
Apart from that, I enjoyed a lot of things from this game, like farming ores, collecting stuff and others. But I can't recommend this game in its current state. It's just the decaying corpse of the real metin2 that died 5 years ago.
If you are new to this game, don't bother with the official servers. Play on a private server, as they are better than the official servers.

I highly recommend the first Bioshock, especially for those who are either new to shooters or for those who enjoy a good game but lack the time (or skill) to devote to hardcore or lengthy gaming.
Keep in mind, this is more of a stealth game, so it is slow. I personally liked the pacing, but if you're looking for a super challenging game with a lot of upbeat action, the first Bioshock isn't for you. If you like a nice RPG with an interesting story and beautiful scenery, though, then you may also enjoy this game.
Bioshock  takes about 21 hours to fully complete if you take your time, which is great for someone like me who enjoys an immersive "full" game experience, but cannot commit much time to gaming.  Another plus of Bioshock is that you may, at any time, adjust the difficulty to suit your level of play.
Although eager to play the Bioshock series, I was hesitant about the first-person perspective making me ill (as previous games, such as Metroid, have done); however, I am delighted to say that was not the case with Bioshock!
Overall,
- the gameplay is wonderfully fun (though a bit repetitive at times), resembling that of horror-survival games;
- the "puzzles" weren't challenging, but still enjoyable;
- the story, though predictable, is quite fascinating;
- the controls were impressively smooth (I used an xbox controller);
- the design and atmosphere (a 40s-style dystopia submerged deep in the ocean) is breathtaking!
